From b67ded2285a60e2353decd18fa8723f7ebad7899 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 10:33:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: halt the VBIF AXI ports before runtime suspend

The DPU runtime suspend drops the clocks and the bus votes and then lets
the MDSS power domain collapse with the VBIF AXI ports never halted.
The downstream SDE driver does not: on every pre-disable power event it
forces the VBIF clock on and requests the AXI halt, waits for the
acknowledgment, and leaves the collapse to clear the request
(sde_kms_handle_power_event() -> sde_vbif_axi_halt_request()).  The GPU
side of this driver does the same with its GBIF before its own collapse
(a6xx_bus_clear_pending_transactions()).

On SM8750 the missing handshake breaks the next power-up, not the
power-down.  The blank itself goes through: the panel off commands are
sent, the DSI hosts power down and the MDSS domain collapses.  After
the domain comes back, the first DSI command DMA never has its data
fetched: CMD_MODE_DMA_BUSY stays set on both links of the bonded pair,
the lanes sit in stop state, the FIFOs are empty, and the transfer
fails with -ETIMEDOUT.  The panel is left uninitialised, the vblank and
commit waits that follow time out, and the screen stays black until
reboot.  The same blank with the domain kept up recovers.  Resetting
the whole MDSS through its BCR on resume does not help, so the state
that goes bad lives on the far side of the AXI port rather than in the
MDSS registers, which is also why the first enable after boot, with no
un-halted collapse before it, always works.

Halt the AXI ports in dpu_runtime_suspend() before the clocks go, where
the VBIF asks for it, and release them in dpu_runtime_resume() before
the memory types are programmed again.  The collapse clears the halt by
itself, so the release only matters when the domain stayed up, but
nothing else would release it then.  A halt that is not acknowledged in
time is reported and the suspend carries on, as downstream does.

In a bounded on-device A/B of the four candidates on this boundary (bus
clocks and votes kept over the collapse, GDSC collapsed without
retention, MDSS reset on resume, AXI halt before the collapse), only
the halt brought the panel back: the halt was acknowledged, the domain
still collapsed, the 122 init commands went out, the next frames were
committed and the DSI status registers read healthy again.

This changes nothing until a catalog entry sets DPU_VBIF_AXI_HALT.

Assisted-by: LLM

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit c343837c783a7e026bb7358460c880026e6aa5d2)
Signed-off-by: Codex <codex@localhost>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_kms.c  |  7 +++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_vbif.c | 36 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_vbif.h |  4 +++
 3 files changed, 47 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_kms.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_kms.c
index 771f61cc98fe..d558e8d560cb 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_kms.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_kms.c
@@ -1453,6 +1453,12 @@ static int __maybe_unused dpu_runtime_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	struct msm_drm_private *priv = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 	struct dpu_kms *dpu_kms = to_dpu_kms(priv->kms);
 
+	/*
+	 * The MDSS power domain may collapse as soon as the clocks are gone;
+	 * halt the VBIF AXI ports first where the hardware asks for it.
+	 */
+	dpu_vbif_axi_halt_request(dpu_kms);
+
 	clk_bulk_disable_unprepare(dpu_kms->num_clocks, dpu_kms->clocks);
 
 	for (i = 0; i < dpu_kms->num_paths; i++)
@@ -1478,6 +1484,7 @@ static int __maybe_unused dpu_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 		return rc;
 	}
 
+	dpu_vbif_axi_halt_release(dpu_kms);
 	dpu_vbif_init_memtypes(dpu_kms);
 
 	drm_for_each_encoder(encoder, ddev)
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_vbif.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_vbif.c
index 0c6fa9bb0cb6..84e1ddd2f217 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_vbif.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_vbif.c
@@ -260,6 +260,42 @@ void dpu_vbif_init_memtypes(struct dpu_kms *dpu_kms)
 	}
 }
 
+/**
+ * dpu_vbif_axi_halt_request - halt the VBIF AXI ports before power collapse
+ * @dpu_kms:	DPU handler
+ *
+ * Requests the halt and waits for it for a bounded time.  A halt that is
+ * not acknowledged is reported but does not hold up the power collapse.
+ */
+void dpu_vbif_axi_halt_request(struct dpu_kms *dpu_kms)
+{
+	struct dpu_hw_vbif *vbif = dpu_kms->hw_vbif;
+
+	if (!vbif || !vbif->ops.set_axi_halt || !vbif->ops.get_axi_halt_status)
+		return;
+
+	vbif->ops.set_axi_halt(vbif, true);
+	if (vbif->ops.get_axi_halt_status(vbif))
+		DPU_ERROR("VBIF AXI ports did not halt before power collapse\n");
+}
+
+/**
+ * dpu_vbif_axi_halt_release - release the VBIF AXI ports after power up
+ * @dpu_kms:	DPU handler
+ *
+ * A power collapse clears the halt on its own; this releases it when the
+ * power domain stayed up.
+ */
+void dpu_vbif_axi_halt_release(struct dpu_kms *dpu_kms)
+{
+	struct dpu_hw_vbif *vbif = dpu_kms->hw_vbif;
+
+	if (!vbif || !vbif->ops.set_axi_halt)
+		return;
+
+	vbif->ops.set_axi_halt(vbif, false);
+}
+
 #ifdef CONFIG_DEBUG_FS
 
 void dpu_debugfs_vbif_init(struct dpu_kms *dpu_kms, struct dentry *debugfs_root)
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_vbif.h b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_vbif.h
index f47a89cb34ea..b97946fb451f 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_vbif.h
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_vbif.h
@@ -44,6 +44,10 @@ void dpu_vbif_clear_errors(struct dpu_kms *dpu_kms);
 
 void dpu_vbif_init_memtypes(struct dpu_kms *dpu_kms);
 
+void dpu_vbif_axi_halt_request(struct dpu_kms *dpu_kms);
+
+void dpu_vbif_axi_halt_release(struct dpu_kms *dpu_kms);
+
 void dpu_debugfs_vbif_init(struct dpu_kms *dpu_kms, struct dentry *debugfs_root);
 
 #endif /* __DPU_VBIF_H__ */
-- 
